hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1093","Ibrahim bin Munqidh bin Abdullah Al-Khawlani told us, Ayoub bin Suwayd told us, on the authority of Utba bin Abi Hakim, on the authority of Abu Sufyan Talha bin Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had promised Abbas a herd of camels, so he sent me He went to him after dinner, and he was in the house of Maimuna bint Al-Harith, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept, and I covered the pillow that he had been pillowing. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he slept not much or much, then he, peace be upon him, got up and performed ablution and performed it well, and it was less A splash of water, then he opened the prayer, so I stood up and performed ablution, so I stood to his left, and he moved his hand back, then he took my ear and made me stand to his right. So he began to say the salaam from every two rak’ahs, and Maimuna was menstruating, so she got up and performed ablution, then she sat behind him, remembering God, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Did your devils make you stay?” She said: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for me, O Messenger of God. Do I have a devil?” May God help me with him, so he converted to Islam. When dawn broke, he stood up and prayed the Witr rak’ah, then he bowed the two rak’ahs of dawn, then he lay on his right side until Bilal came to him and called him to prayer.”"
